Apple released the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-announces-iphone-18-pro-and-iphone-18-pro-max/">iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max</a> in September 2026, five years after the iPhone 13 Pro and iPhone 13 Pro Max. The 2021 models introduced ProMotion displays, macro photography, a 3x Telephoto camera, and substantially longer battery life than their predecessors. They remain capable phones and support <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, but owners now have five generations of upgrades to consider.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-13-pro-vs-iphone-18-pro.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068625" /><br/>
The iPhone 14 Pro brought the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, an Always-On display, a 48-megapixel Main camera, and Emergency SOS via satellite. The iPhone 15 Pro introduced the Action button and USB-C. The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-16/">iPhone 16</a> Pro added larger displays, the Camera Control, a 48-megapixel Ultra Wide camera, and expanded video capabilities.<br/>
<br/>
The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a> Pro adopted an aluminum unibody with vapor chamber cooling and upgraded the Telephoto and front-facing cameras. This year's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> adds the A20 Pro chip, a variable-aperture Main camera, a smaller &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj;, and further gains in battery life and charging speed. For an iPhone 13 Pro owner, these changes accumulate across nearly every part of the phone.<br/>
<br/>
In the United States, the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-18-pro-pricing/">starts at &#36;1,199</a> and the Pro Max at &#36;1,299, each with 256GB of storage. That is &#36;200 more than the corresponding iPhone 13 Pro model's 2021 starting price, although the older phones started with 128GB. Apple no longer sells the iPhone 13 Pro, so anyone buying one now will be looking at a used or refurbished device. Here are the key differences:<br/>
